1ym|n|To support, either by furnishing strength or means in cooperation to effect a purpose, or to prevent or to remove evil; to help; to assist. ; Help; succor; assistance; relief. ; The person or thing that promotes or helps in something done; a helper; an assistant. ; A subsidy granted to the king by Parliament; also, an exchequer loan. ; A pecuniary tribute paid by a vassal to his lord on special occasions. ; An aid-de-camp, so called by abbreviation; as, a general's aid.	a:2c0n,78,7;tqt,50,4;1030,42,2;1d4d,42,2;ybb,39,3;ufe,31,56;20y7,26,4;13d,17,3;1lk2,12,4~ufe,31,56;2c0n,78,7;1lk2,12,4;20y7,26,4;tqt,50,4;13d,17,3;ybb,39,3;1d4d,42,2;1030,42,2	v:1030,79,26;2c0n,50,1~1030,79,26;2c0n,50,1	n:1030,76,21;1d4d,48,3;254p,22,6;2gt7,16,14;243a,11,4~1030,76,21;2gt7,16,14;254p,22,6;243a,11,4;1d4d,48,3	N:1ifg,48,19;1aej,47,1;1seq,38,3;22px,36,6;1r8n,27,7;4bp,4,6~1ifg,48,19;1r8n,27,7;22px,36,6;4bp,4,6;1seq,38,3;1aej,47,1
